+/// `%::z` (`+hh:mm:ss`) and `%:::z` (`+hh`) are listed among the specifiers "available both to
+/// formatting and parsing", but the parser reads `+hh:mm` for both: the text `%::z` writes is
+/// `TooLong`, the text `%:::z` writes is `TooShort`. KNOWN FAILURE chrono/1.
+#[hegel::test]
+fn offset_specifiers_with_seconds_or_hours_only_parse_back(tc: hegel::TestCase) {
